      "start_seconds": 1.11,
      "end_seconds": 4.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.96,
      "end_seconds": 13.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.73,
      "end_seconds": 28.88,
      "duration_seconds": 13.15,
      "text": "Actually, uh, mainly sudden severe pain in the lower tummy. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.51,
      "end_seconds": 35.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.74,
      "end_seconds": 49.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.43,
      "end_seconds": 75.26,
      "duration_seconds": 15.83,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 104 over 58, respiratory rate 16, pulse is 99 beats a minute, temperature 37.2, height 186 centimetres, weight 97 kilos. How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.83,
      "end_seconds": 85.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "Probably three weeks. Yeah. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.89,
      "end_seconds": 89.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Right, how often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.9,
      "end_seconds": 113.89,
      "duration_seconds": 22.99,
      "text": "Honestly, a few times a day. Yeah, as for shoulder tip pain, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. Well, I did have vaginal spotting at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.5,
      "end_seconds": 117.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "A few quick ones: discharge, vomiting or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.89,
      "end_seconds": 126.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "None of those, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.81,
      "end_seconds": 130.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Any rashes or skin problems otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.29,
      "end_seconds": 132.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.05,
      "end_seconds": 137.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.04,
      "end_seconds": 141.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.1,
      "end_seconds": 144.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.84,
      "end_seconds": 150.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Yeah, you know, I've had an underactive thyroid, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.33,
      "end_seconds": 162.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.2,
      "end_seconds": 166.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.1,
      "end_seconds": 171.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.51,
      "end_seconds": 184.72,
      "duration_seconds": 11.21,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. I walk the dog every morning. I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.85,
      "end_seconds": 195.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.78,
      "end_seconds": 203.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.57,
      "text": "Years back I got hives from amoxicillin, so I stay away from it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.65,
      "end_seconds": 218.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Is there any regular medication you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.05,
      "end_seconds": 221.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "No, none."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.39,
      "end_seconds": 225.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.34,
      "end_seconds": 227.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.15,
      "end_seconds": 243.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "You are pale and clammy with a rigid, tender tummy and a very low blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.82,
      "end_seconds": 249.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.71,
      "end_seconds": 269.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: It fits best with a ruptured ectopic pregnancy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.53,
      "end_seconds": 274.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.15,
      "end_seconds": 313.11,
      "duration_seconds": 33.96,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a ruptured ectopic pregnancy, but I'd like to confirm. Let's book urgent blood tests to look into internal bleeding. We should do a pregnancy test for collapse. I am calling the emergency team, you need an operation now. Please don't wait if the symptoms get worse. That's when to be seen urgently. Let's plan a check straight away. Okay, does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.1,
      "end_seconds": 319.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Right, uh, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.69,
      "end_seconds": 321.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}